<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετοίχομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go after, go in quest of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούσδε μετοιχόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.111
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆρυξ δὲ μετῴχετο θεῖον ἀοιδόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.47
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. rei, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετέρχομαι</span>
			 IV.<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαρμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1332
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> with hostile
			intent, <i>rush upon, pursue</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δ᾽ Ἄβαντα μετῴχετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.148
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>go among</i> or <i>through</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὰ ἄστυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.7
				</span></i>
			 (or in signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>follow behind</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς τοι . .
				μετοιχομένη φάος οἴσει</span>; <i><span class="en">
				19.24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
